/td></tr></tbody></table>", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "False", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "insignia", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "pd", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}}]}, "10315951": {"pageid": 10315951, "ns": 6, "title": "File:Flag of Morocco (1666\u20131915).svg", "imagerepository": "local", "imageinfo": [{"url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Flag_of_Morocco_%281666%E2%80%931915%29.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Morocco_(1666%E2%80%931915).svg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=10315951", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2011-12-04 05:36:17", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "Flag of Morocco (1666\u20131915)", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Self-published work|PD-self|Plain red SVG flag icons|Citation templates using deprecated parameters|SVG historical flags of Morocco|SVG red flags|Solid red flags", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "Flag of Morocco during the rule of the Alaouite dynasty (17-20).", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "2008-08", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<p>Own work by uploader - \n</p>\n<ul><li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">EL, Noble Timothy Myers- (30 December 2004)    (in English)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=H8tMuh9MyTsC&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;pg=PA67&amp;dq=empire+of+morocco+flag+red&amp;hl=fr\">The Huevolution of Sacred Muur Science Past and Present: A Theoretical Compilation</a></i>, Author House  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-4184-6949-8\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-1-4184-6949-8\">978-1-4184-6949-8</a>. </small></cite>: <i>\"Interesting enough 1912 was the year the green 5-pointed star was put in the center of the all red Moroccan flag\".</i></li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">Minahan, James (2010)    (in English)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=qM5XAAAAYAAJ&amp;newbks=0&amp;hl=fr\">The Complete Guide to National Symbols and Emblems</a></i>, Greenwood Press, pp.\u00a0617  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-313-34500-5\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-313-34500-5\">978-0-313-34500-5</a>. </small></cite>: <i>\"The flag of Morocco before 1915 was a plain red field\"</i>.</li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">(in English) (1907) <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=UBlJAQAAMAAJ&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;q=empire+of+morocco+flag+red&amp;hl=fr\">Railway Conductors' Monthly</a></i>, pp.\u00a0631  <small></small></cite>: <i>\"In nation's index the red flag stand for Morocco, an Empire or Sultanate, in the northwestern part of Africa\"</i>.</li>\n<li>\u201cChapter 9. The First 'Red Flag'\u201d, in <cite>The Half-Lives of Pat Lowther</cite><sup><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.3138/9781442681422-012\">[1]</a></sup>, University of Toronto Press, <span class=\"mw-formatted-date\" title=\"2005-01-31\">2005-01-31</span>, pages 134</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><i>\"The Alawite dynasty first adopted a red flag for Morocco in the 17th century . Red symbolizes the royal family\"</i>.</dd></dl>\n<ul><li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">(in English)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=X9kcBzjUtrwC&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;pg=PA10&amp;dq=red+flag+moroccan+state+countries+and+their+culture&amp;hl=fr\">The Report: Emerging Morocco 2007</a></i>, Oxford Business Group, pp.\u00a010  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-902339-76-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-1-902339-76-4\">978-1-902339-76-4</a>. </small></cite>: <i>\"FLAG: The Moroccan flag is red with a Solomon's seal, a five-pointed star outlined in green. The red flag was introduced by the Alaouite dynasty in the beginning of the 17th century. The Sulayman star was introduced in 1912 to distinguish the country's flag from others. Green and red are colours associated with Islam\".</i></li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">Bowen, Patrick D. (11 September 2017)    (in English)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=WPA0DwAAQBAJ&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;pg=PA26&amp;dq=red+flag+moroccan+state+countries+and+their+culture&amp;hl=fr\">A History of Conversion to Islam in the United States, Volume 2: The African American Islamic Renaissance, 1920-1975</a></i>, BRILL, pp.\u00a026  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-90-04-35437-1\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-90-04-35437-1\">978-90-04-35437-1</a>. </small></cite>: <i>\"It is worth noting, too, that in the late seventeenth century, Morocco's Muslim Alaouite dynasty adopted for its country's symbol the plain red flag, which had been used for hundreds of years by various Muslim communities, but was not at that time the symbol of another major African country\"</i>.</li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">Piquet, Victor (1918)    (in French)  <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=XwQ_AQAAMAAJ&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;dq=empire+ch%C3%A9rifien+rouge+drapeau&amp;q=empire+ch%C3%A9rifien+rouge+drapeau&amp;hl=fr\">Le Maroc: g\u00e9ographie--histoire--mise en valeur ...</a></i>, A. Colin, pp.\u00a0263  <small></small></cite>: <i>\"The flag of the Sharifian Empire, which was completely red, has been, since the end of 1915, red with a green star in the shape of Solomon's ring\"</i>.</li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">(in French) (1906) <i> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=9U5SAAAAYAAJ&amp;newbks=0&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;dq=empire+ch%C3%A9rifien+rouge+drapeau&amp;q=empire+ch%C3%A9rifien+rouge+drapeau&amp;hl=fr\">L'illustration</a></i>, J. Dubochet, pp.\u00a0432  <small></small></cite>: \"<i>...l'\u00e9tendard rouge - sang de l'empire ch\u00e9rifien\"</i>.</li></ul>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Library_digitised_image_from_page_337_of_%22Orient_Line_Guide,_etc._(Fifth_edition-_re-written.)%22.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title='Moroccan flag in \"British Library digitised image from page 337 of \"Orient Line Guide\"'><img alt='Moroccan flag in \"British Library digitised image from page 337 of \"Orient Line Guide\"' src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/British_Library_digitised_image_from_page_337_of_%22Orient_Line_Guide%2C_etc._%28Fifth_edition-_re-written.%29%22.jpg/120px-British_Library_digitised_image_from_page_337_of_%22Orient_Line_Guide%2C_etc._%28Fifth_edition-_re-written.%29%22.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"95\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/British_Library_digitised_image_from_page_337_of_%22Orient_Line_Guide%2C_etc._%28Fifth_edition-_re-written.%29%22.jpg/250px-British_Library_digitised_image_from_page_337_of_%22Orient_Line_Guide%2C_etc._%28Fifth_edition-_re-written.%29%22.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1775\" data-file-height=\"2246\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Moroccan flag in \"British Library digitised image from page 337 of \"Orient Line Guide\"</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flags_of_the_world_1911.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title='Moroccan flag in \"Flags of the world 1911\"'><img alt='Moroccan flag in \"Flags of the world 1911\"' src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flags_of_the_world_1911.jpg/120px-Flags_of_the_world_1911.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"76\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flags_of_the_world_1911.jpg/250px-Flags_of_the_world_1911.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1576\" data-file-height=\"2471\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Moroccan flag in \"Flags of the world 1911\"</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_encyclopedia_world_flag_chart_published_in_1904_(Etsy)_01.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title='Moroccan flag in \"United States encyclopedia world flag chart published in 1904\"'><img alt='Moroccan flag in \"United States encyclopedia world flag chart published in 1904\"' src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/United_States_encyclopedia_world_flag_chart_published_in_1904_%28Etsy%29_01.jpg/120px-United_States_encyclopedia_world_flag_chart_published_in_1904_%28Etsy%29_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"99\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/United_States_encyclopedia_world_flag_chart_published_in_1904_%28Etsy%29_01.jpg/250px-United_States_encyclopedia_world_flag_chart_published_in_1904_%28Etsy%29_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1588\" data-file-height=\"1304\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Moroccan flag in \"United States encyclopedia world flag chart published in 1904\"</div>\n\t\t</li>\n</ul>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Flad\" title=\"User:Flad\">Flad</a>", "source": 